<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bogdan I of Moldavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1367</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bogdan I was a Romanian voivode from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maramures">Maramureș</a> who, having quarrelled with the Hungarian crown, crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a> around 1359, drove out the descendants of Dragoș and made Moldavia independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. He ruled until about 1367. His successors ruled Moldavia for two centuries, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> later called the country Kara Boğdan, 'Black Bogdania', after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bogdan-i-of-moldavia.jpg" alt="Bogdan I of Moldavia" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.crestinortodox.ro/biserici-manastiri/manastirea-bogdana-67925.html · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bogdan_I_of_Moldova_mural.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
